  (o) `frameToSpectra_` line 213: `spec.reserve(n / wins.size() + 64)` fine. Line 217: IM band filter `k0 < win.im_lo || k0 > win.im_hi` — MS1 win im band ±1e9 fine.

  (p) MS1 from mzpeak: `wins[i] = {MzPeakWin{0,0,-1e9,1e9}}` then setMSLevel(1) since !(0<0) ✓. But then in the consumer, consumeMS1Spectrum_ gets it. In `run()`, the handoff calls `consumer.consumeSpectrum(spec)` — FullSwathFileConsumer::consumeSpectrum dispatches by MS level presumably ✓.

  (q) Exception safety in `MzPeakExactMz` ctor: `std::remove(tmpl)` not called on throw paths (leaks temp file) — minor. Also mkstemp file created with fd, closed, then fopen "wb" — ok.

  (r) `readMember_` footer: `uint32_t flen; memcpy(&flen, tail.data(), 4)` — parquet footer length; then `readMember_(z, ..., st.size - 8 - flen, flen)` — if flen is corrupt (larger than st.size), `from` negative → zip_int64_t negative → `if (from > 0 && zip_fseek...)` skipped, len huge → `std::vector<char> buf((size_t)len)` → massive allocation/throw. Fail-closed-ish (throws bad_alloc) but ugly. Low.

