  (t) OpenMP nested levels: `omp_set_max_active_levels(2)` only when n_bands > 1; the inner precursor loop (p_team) is nested inside the window loop — with max_active_levels default 1, nested parallel for runs SERIAL (p_team=1 effectively? No — num_threads(p_team) with nested parallelism disabled → serialized team of 1). If n_bands == 1 (user sets perf:trace_bands 1), max_active_levels stays default → inner precursor parallel-for is inactive → serial scoring. But also detectTraces_ banding off. That's intended-ish. But when n_bands>1, active levels 2 → both inner band loop AND precursor loop can be active; both divide budget. OK.

