  Q5: tests. tests/ has calibration C++ golden tests, calibration python, entrapment python. Nothing for DIAPseudoSpectra itself. Smallest high-value test set:
  1. inferPrecursors_ unit test: synthetic MS1 trace set — a z=2 envelope (mono + M+1 + M+2 at 1.00335/2 spacing, co-eluting, same IM) plus a decoy peak one spacing below with low intensity; assert mono_mz/charge and that isotope peaks don't seed their own precursors; test break-on-first-miss (gap at M+1, present M+2 → count mode stops; envelope mode spans); test tie-break toward low z; test used[] de-isotoping count.
  2. findPartner/lower_bound edge: empty ms1 vector, single trace, partner exactly at tolerance boundary (off-by-one at tol edge — lower_bound(target-tol)/upper_bound(target+tol) inclusive).
  3. min_charge gate predicate test: precursors with charge 0/1/2 at zmin=2 → charge-0 survives, z=1 dropped; and ordering: require_isotope_support then min_charge.
  4. winKey quantization: two windows or precursor at edge — test that precursor at win edge routes consistently (or just assert the quantization behavior is documented).
  5. compactify round-trip: NaN/inf/out-of-range peaks dropped and counted; mz exactly at 4.2e9/1e5 boundary.
  6. xicCorr: n<5 → 0; constant series → 0; perfect co-elution → 1.
  7. FragGrid: build from traces, assert off sentinel, invnorm 0 for constant trace; overflow guard.
  8. Determinism smoke: run tool on a tiny synthetic mzML (a few frames) at threads 1 vs 8, compare semantic digest — they have bench/semantic_digest.py; add a tiny synthetic input so CI can run it.
  9. assembleFromList_ cap: max_fragments partial_sort with ties deterministic.
  10. selftest_wavelet exists but isn't run in CI — wire diag:selftest_wavelet into CI (it's already a self-test that ships; tests.yml doesn't run it presumably since tool isn't built in CI).

  Is current verification sufficient? No: whole-file benchmarks + peptide-set gate catch regressions on ONE instrument/cohort and can't run in CI; nothing tests the code paths not exercised by defaults (envelope scoring, rp_max, merge, consolidate, mzpeak loader) — several of which have already shipped broken (E5 bypass, consolidate IM gate, auto-band-fix serial tracing). Those three defects are precisely the class unit tests would catch.

